# AIFRED Intelligence Layer — Build Plan

[AIFRED GitHub repository](https://github.com/kaeganscott26/AIFRED?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

First: understand what you're actually building

The architecture already defines this pipeline:

DAW audio
    ↓
shared DSP analyzer
    ↓
EngineSnapshot
    ↓
BufferHunter
    ↓
ObservationSnapshot
    ↓
aifred_filter
    ↓
FilteredMixContext
    ↓
=============================
      INTELLIGENCE LAYER
=============================
    ↓
IntelligenceCore
    ↓
context assembly
    ↓
read-only tools
    ↓
evidence/policy
    ↓
provider
    ↓
structured response
    ↓
validated user-facing answer

That boundary is very important.

The intelligence layer does not analyze raw audio.

It does not calculate LUFS.

It does not calculate crest factor.

It does not invent DSP measurements.

It receives FilteredMixContext and reasons about what the existing DSP system already measured. That's explicitly the architecture law in the repo.

So your first mental model should be:

> DSP tells AIFRED what is happening. Intelligence figures out what that means.



That's the whole game.


