STEP 6 — Give yourself a ContextBuilder

Conceptually:

class ContextBuilder
{
public:

    ContextPacket build(
        const IntelligenceRequest& request
    );
};

Internally it should do something like:

receive request
    ↓
validate observation
    ↓
validate profile
    ↓
validate reference
    ↓
determine relevant evidence
    ↓
select fields
    ↓
attach provenance
    ↓
enforce size budget
    ↓
return ContextPacket

Critical rule

The context builder does not interpret.

It selects.

That's important.

Bad:

if (bassIsWeak)
    packet.problem = "weak bass";

Good:

packet.add(
    EvidenceRef{
        "FilteredMixContext",
        "lowFrequencyEnergy",
        observationId
    }
);

Let policy/reasoning determine what that means.


