---

STEP 19 — Then build the failure tests

This is where I'd spend a LOT of time.

Test:

No observation

"I don't have enough valid observation data to assess that."

Stale observation

"The available measurement is stale, so I can't make a reliable current-mix claim."

Incompatible reference

"I can't make a reference comparison from the current reference state."

Unknown plugin cause

"I can identify the measured behavior, but not which plugin caused it."

No problem

"The available evidence doesn't indicate a correction is needed."

Model hallucination

Provider says:

Your Pro-Q 3 at 3.2 kHz is causing the harshness.

but no plugin data exists.

Validator should kill that claim.


